from lib import *
P('an-don','An Đồn'); P('ba-ria','Bà Rịa'); P('nhi-binh','Nhị Bình'); P('hanh-thong-tay','Hạnh Thông Tây'); P('camp-e-se-pich','Camp Ê-sê-pích'); P('plei-can','Plây Cần')
D='vietnam-hanoi'; OP=['vietnam-operations']
E('r5-spring','1969-02-23','Feb. 23–Mar. 31','Region V\'s three forces hit the American strategic depots at An Đồn, Đà Nẵng, Đèo Son and Miếu Lỗ near Quy Nhơn, and Cam Ranh, and the command posts of the III Marine Amphibious Force, the 23d (Americal) Division and the 11th, 196th and 198th Brigades. The 2d Division draws American mobile forces out to An Hòa, Quảng Đà, Tiên Phước, Quảng Nam, and west of Tư Nghĩa and Đức Phổ, Quảng Ngãi. By the history\'s count thousands of the enemy out of action, hundreds of aircraft and vehicles destroyed. AFP, Mar. 14, quotes Lt. Gen. Hoàng Xuân Lãm: the fighting around Đà Nẵng shows the Viet Cong infrastructure intact.','103–5',also=OP,place='da-nang',us=True,ntags=['name:hoang-xuan-lam'],names=['Hoàng Xuân Lãm'],see='cal.1969-02-22.vietnam-hanoi',check='the first day, which the history gives as the spring phase\'s opening, the night of Feb. 22–23; the figures.',lw='Region V, spring phase: depots and command posts')
E('esepic','1969-02','Feb., spring phase','Camp Ê-sê-pích, Bình Thuận. Main force and local guerrillas raid the base: a battalion of the American 101st Airborne badly hurt, two artillery companies, 13 aircraft destroyed. The history calls it the spring phase\'s best action on the far southern coast of Trung Bộ.','105',also=OP,place='camp-e-se-pich',us=True,at='after 1969-02-22',see='cal.1969-02-22.vietnam-hanoi',check='the day; the history gives the phase, Feb. 23–Mar. 31, and the camp\'s name as printed.',lw='Camp Ê-sê-pích raided')
E('highlands-spring','1969-02','Feb., spring phase','Central Highlands. After beating Bình Tây 48 to 50, the three forces attack the line west of Kon Tum: the bases at Plây Cần and Kleng and Đức Cơ in Gia Lai. Under artillery, main force, local forces and guerrillas fight hand to hand for hills and valleys against American air and artillery. Sappers strike deep at the rear of the 1st Brigade, 4th Division at Tân Phú and Buôn Ma Thuột.','104–5',also=OP,place='plei-can',us=True,at='after 1969-02-22',see='cal.1969-02-22.vietnam-hanoi',check='the days; the history says "những tháng đầu năm 1969" and so places the fighting before the summer phase.',lw='Central Highlands: Plây Cần, Kleng, Đức Cơ')
E('danquyen','1969-05-11','May 11','Kon Tum. Under the Đắk Tô 2 attack Saigon opens operation Dân Quyền northwest of the town with eight infantry battalions and three armored squadrons, to stretch the attackers. The enemy avoids contact and holds hilltops; the Front\'s command sends staff down to the units to carry out a new plan, pursuing day and night and surrounding each force found.','120–21',also=OP,place='kontum',see='cal.1969-05-11.vietnam-hanoi',check='the day; the history puts it after the night of May 10–11.',lw='Operation Dân Quyền northwest of Kon Tum')
E('navy-mid','1969','1969, mid','The Navy Command, which is also the Northeast Military Region\'s, reorganizes the naval force: some units are split off or merged into battalions directly under the command, to fight alone or with others in assigned waters, ready the field for the Navy\'s mobile force and help in coastal militia building. In 1970 the Central Military Party Committee\'s standing body separates the Navy from the Northeast Military Region.','205–6',at='before 1969-05',vis=True,check='the day; the history says "từ giữa năm 1969".',lw='Navy Command reorganizes its naval force')
E('ho-79','1969-05-19','May 19','Hồ Chí Minh, receiving a delegation of the army cadres\' class come to wish him long life on his 79th birthday, speaks on the strength of the war: a one-kilogram weight, set at an advantage, lifts a hundred; the Americans lose by their position, though still stubborn. His charge: the rear to do better for the front, first of all; build forces of high quality, vigilant and ready, and spare men, arms and rice; the troops to help the people and strengthen the rear.','192 and n. 1–2',place='hanoi',ntags=['name:ho-chi-minh'],names=['Hồ Chí Minh'],see='cal.1969-05.vietnam-hanoi',tocheck='Hồ Chí Minh, *Toàn tập*, XII (2000), 455, 465–66 (cited by [[w.lich-su-khang-chien-chong-my]], VI, 192 n.).',check='the day; the history gives the occasion, his 79th birthday, and its own date for the birthday is May 19 (VI, 117).',lw='Hồ Chí Minh talks to the army class on his birthday')
E('balangan','1969','1969','Ba Làng An, Quảng Ngãi. 6,000 villagers forced by the Saigon side into a concentration area press the struggle until they are sent back to their old villages.','127–28 and n. 1',also=['vietnam-pacification'],place='quang-ngai-province',check='the day; the history gives it among the results of the spring and summer phases of 1969.',tocheck='Viện Nghiên cứu chủ nghĩa Mác–Lênin và Tư tưởng Hồ Chí Minh, *Lịch sử Đảng Cộng sản Việt Nam, 1954–1975* (Chính trị quốc gia, 1995), II, 440–41 (cited by [[w.lich-su-khang-chien-chong-my]], VI, 128 n.).',lw='Ba Làng An villagers returned to their villages')
E('mai-dinh','1969','1969','Hạnh Thông Tây, Gò Vấp. The Mai Dinh sapper team of Saigon–Gia Định Battalion 4 slips into the depot, sets charges and destroys 35,000 tons of munitions. Mai Dinh is later named a Hero of the Liberation Armed Forces.','140 and n. 1',also=OP,place='hanh-thong-tay',us=False,check='the day and the year; the history gives the raid in its account of the autumn and winter fighting round Saigon.',lw='Mai Dinh team destroys the Hạnh Thông Tây depot')
E('nhi-binh','1969','1969','Nhị Bình. Battalion 2 of the Quyết Thắng Regiment shoots down 15 helicopters in beating a sweep.','140',also=OP,place='nhi-binh',check='the district, which the history prints "Gò Môn"; the day and the year, which it gives with the Saigon-area fighting of 1969.',lw='Quyết Thắng Battalion 2 downs 15 helicopters at Nhị Bình')
E('group10','1969','1969','Rừng Sác. Group 10, the sappers, fights encircled through the year with 300 killed, cut off from supply and from its contacts among the people; makes its own arms, finds a way to attack ships, and raids the Nhà Bè fuel depot and the Thành Tuy Hạ bomb depot. By early 1970 170 are left.','140 and n. 2',also=OP,place='rung-sat',see='cal.1969-05-19.vietnam-hanoi',check='the days of the raids; the history gives the year.',lw='Group 10 in 1969: Nhà Bè and Thành Tuy Hạ raids')
E('baria','1969-12','Dec., winter','Bà Rịa. Against the Australian brigade\'s half-buried bunkers and fences, the province Party committee orders "Three holds": the Party holds the people, the people the land, the armed forces the enemy. Attacks from outside fail; scouts and sappers then slip in and build agents and secret guerrillas. One night Battalion 445 and Company 25 of Long Đất destroy 12 bunkers. By early 1970 the bunker tactic is beaten.','142–43 and n. 1',also=OP,place='ba-ria',at='before 1969-12-21',polity='drv',check='the days; the history gives the winter phase and the early 1970 result.',lw='Bà Rịa: "Three holds" and the bunkers')
E('vna-land','1969-11-03','Nov. 3','The Vietnam News Agency\'s commentary "Cải cách điền địa - một trò bịp bợm và phản động" (Land reform, a fraud and a reactionary trick), on the Saigon government\'s land program: nearly all land in the South, from landlords\' to the French-owned land sold to Diệm and Nhu in 1958, has been divided by the revolution to the peasants since the uprising; Saigon\'s village officials and exiled landlords take it back and give it to puppet troops, in Long An, Tây Ninh, Bình Thuận and Bà Rịa.','49–50',place='hanoi',check='the place; the history names the agency, not the city, and gives the day only.',lw='Vietnam News Agency on Saigon land reform')
E('laird-0114','1970-01-14','Jan. 14','Laird, in a speech in California: of all the changes of policy in the administration\'s first year none matters more than Vietnamization, the test of the wider Asian policy Nixon announced at Guam in July 1969.','29 and n. 2',th='vietnam',polity='us',ntags=['name:laird-melvin-r'],names=['Laird'],ok=['ok:fields-place'],check='the words and the place; the history quotes in Vietnamese and gives "Caliphoócnia".',lw='Laird on Vietnamization, in California')
dump('o5.yaml')
